WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.038
SPEAKER:<i> We were ordinary women
 trying to save women's lives,</i>

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.839
but we were criminals.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:08.475
<i> We were felons.</i>

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:14.113
<i> For most of the nation in '72,
 abortion was illegal.</i>

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.481
SPEAKER 2:
<i> We had to go underground.</i>

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.884
SPEAKER 3:
<i> The woman would be given
 the address to the front.</i>

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:22.822
SPEAKER 4:<i> It was probably
 obvious to neighbors</i>

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.124
what was going on.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.594
SPEAKER 5:
<i> We came to the surface
 from other things...</i>

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:31.230 line:0%
<i> the anti-war movement,
 the civil rights movement.</i>

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.199
SPEAKER 6:
<i> You couldn't not pay attention</i>

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.667
to what was going on.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.969
Fetal death is murder.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.971
SPEAKER 3:<i> You could not work
 as a pregnant woman.</i>

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.807
SPEAKER 7:
<i> If you weren't married,
 you were out of luck.</i>

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.176
They were terrible situations.

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:47.247
The septic abortion ward
was full every day.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.681
SPEAKER:
<i> Women did awful things.</i>

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:52.452
<i> They were literally dying
 because they were women.</i>

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.020
So we thought,
"We can be of use."

00:00:55.821 --> 00:00:58.892
I said, "We could use my phone,
but change it

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.294
so that they don't ask
for Eleanor.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.763
How about Jane?
Nobody's called Jane anymore."

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.031
SPEAKER 8:
<i> We hid the phone numbers
 on bulletin boards</i>

00:01:06.131 --> 00:01:08.635
around Chicago.
"Pregnant? Call Jane."

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:12.939
The clientele included
daughters, wives, mistresses

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.441
<i> of police, states' attorneys,
 judges.</i>

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:19.579
SPEAKER 9:<i> It dawned on me
 how big an issue this was.</i>

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.913
♪ ("FEARLESS"
BY KAT LEON PLAYS) ♪

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.449
<i> ♪ Go on
 Take a stab at my heart ♪</i>

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.217
SPEAKER 10:<i> Jane was
 an outrageous undertaking</i>

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.752
<i> by a lot of smart women.</i>

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.121
I was not there
to pass judgment.

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:31.091
SPEAKER 3:
<i>I knew there were women like me.</i>

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:35.228
Under the radar
of the Chicago Mafia

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.262
<i> and the police department.</i>

00:01:37.362 --> 00:01:38.798
We were all being watched.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.135
The phone rings. A man says,
"We know where you are."

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.671
SPEAKER 11:<i> There were
 11 counts of conspiracy</i>

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.874
<i> to commit abortion,
 110 years for each of us.</i>

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.108
So that's a long time.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.344
That might have ended Jane
right then and there.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:56.149
<i> ♪ 'Cause I'm fearless
 Fearless, fearless ♪</i>

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.018
I couldn't see myself
sitting on the sidelines.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.155
SPEAKER:
<i> We were building a new world,</i>

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.489
<i> one woman at a time.</i>

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:06.926
<i> ♪ Come on, test this, baby
 I'm reckless ♪</i>

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.563
SPEAKER 13:
<i> Sometimes you have to stand up
 to legitimate authority,</i>

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.299
and sometimes
there are unjust laws

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.634
<i> that need to be challenged.</i>

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.102
<i> ♪ And you're never gonna
 Break me ♪</i>

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.872
<i> ♪ Never gonna shake me down ♪</i>

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.676 line:0%
<i> ♪ Whoa ♪</i>

